% c081 (A&S Unit 3, PDF 54-56: dissonance is brief and unaccented; an anticipation sounds before the strong beat and is restruck on it, Ex. 3-20): 254 Hn 4 D4 -> C4 on beat 3 (was D4 whole note), so the S head's anticipated C4 (Hn 1-2, Vla, Cl 2) no longer grinds a major 2nd against D4 in the horns for a half note; beat 3 is F-A-C over G (IV over V, no V-I), and Hn 4's C4 is restruck at 255.
